$ PEP 3116 - New I/O

Any object that provides `read()` or `write()` is a stream-like object.
-
This PEP addresses useful ("exotic") functions like `readline()` or `seek()` (which may or may not be available in a stream-like object).

The new I/O spec is intended to be similar ot the Java I/O libraries.

There are three I/O layers, each of which as an abstract base class:
  • Raw (Unit is a byte)
  • Buffered (for sequential access, `flush()` is a noop)
  • Text (Unit is a character)

